<title>PORTUGAL: Sonae, Multiplan sell shopping centre hldg.</title>
<headline>Sonae, Multiplan sell shopping centre hldg.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese group Sonae Imobiliaria and Japeth, a unit of Brazilian group Multiplan, each sold a 25 percent stake in the Cascais shopping complex near Lisbon, a statement said.</p>
<p>The buyers are TransEuropean Property Limited Partnership II and the PanEuropean Property Unit Trust, which each acquired 25 percent stakes.</p>
<p>&quot;The value of the transaction was based on a valuation of CascaisShopping of 16 billion escudos,&quot; the statement said. It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
